# Backlog row 37: the DirectML provider against the CPU provider on this machine,
# 2026-11-26.
#
# Runtime: a scratch venv with onnxruntime-directml 1.23.0 (providers
# DmlExecutionProvider, CPUExecutionProvider), numpy, onnx. Machine: RTX 3060,
# i7-8700K, Windows 11. 20 iterations after 3 warm-up runs, median of wall clock,
# one process per model. The script is .validation/bench-dml.py: same input
# (RandomState(7)), the output of both providers compared element-wise.
#
# The first model is the one this repository ships, templates/onnx-inference-ofx/
# models/test_conv.onnx (opset 17, one 3-channel convolution); the second is the
# 128-channel two-convolution model the CUDA numbers in section 5 use.
#
# 1. the shipped model
onnxruntime 1.23.0 | templates/onnx-inference-ofx/models/test_conv.onnx
available ['DmlExecutionProvider', 'CPUExecutionProvider']

